# 1. DEFINITIONS

For the purposes of this Agreement:

### 1.1 "Project" or "Program"

means the mod project identified above, including its original code, scripts, configuration files, documentation, artwork, graphics, textures, models, sounds, music, writing, designs, localization files, tools, development files, and other materials created specifically for the Project, together with any Contributions incorporated into it.

The terms "Project" and "Program" are used interchangeably in this Agreement where the context permits.

### 1.2 "Contribution"

means any code, script, artwork, texture, model, sound, music, writing, design, localization, documentation, configuration, concept, asset, fix, modification, or other material created, submitted, or developed by a Contributor specifically for the Project.

### 1.3 "Contributor"

means any person or entity that creates, submits, develops, or otherwise provides a Contribution to the Project.

### 1.4 "Recipient"

means any person or entity that receives, downloads, accesses, subscribes to, obtains, or otherwise comes into possession of the Project or any part of it.

### 1.5 "Derivative Work"

means a work based upon, derived from, incorporating, or substantially incorporating any part of the Project, except to the extent that such work consists solely of materials independently owned by a third party and not derived from the Project.

### 1.6 "Modified Work"

means any work resulting from the addition to, deletion from, alteration of, modification of, or incorporation of any part of the Project.

### 1.7 "Distribute"

means providing, publishing, uploading, sharing, transferring, mirroring, repackaging, hosting, or otherwise making the Project or any part of it available to another person or entity.

### 1.8 "Source Code"

means source code and other development files in a form reasonably suitable for modification, including scripts, configuration files, documentation, build files, and related development materials.

### 1.9 "Team Leader"

means the owner and rights holder of the Project's original content and the person or entity authorized to administer the Project and grant permissions under this Agreement.

The Team Leader is the sole Project authority for granting permissions on behalf of the Project, except to the extent that a particular right belongs to a third party or is governed by mandatory law or the terms of a platform or service.

### 1.10 "Project Materials"

means all materials in the Project that are owned or controlled by the Team Leader, including original Contributions that have been validly assigned to the Team Leader under this Agreement.

### 1.11 "Third-Party Content"

means any material incorporated into, used by, derived from, or distributed with the Project that is owned by a person or entity other than the Team Leader, including but not limited to game assets, trademarks, software, libraries, fonts, music, artwork, sounds, models, or other intellectual property.

Third-Party Content remains subject to the rights, licenses, and restrictions of its respective rights holder.

