## 5.1 Public Repository

The Project may be distributed through a public GitHub repository.

Publication of the Project on GitHub does not, by itself, grant a general third-party license to reuse, modify, redistribute, repackage, or commercially exploit the Project Materials.

## 5.2 GitHub Platform Rights

Because GitHub is an external platform, use of the Project through GitHub is also subject to the GitHub Terms of Service and the rights that GitHub provides to its users through its platform functionality.

For example, GitHub's current Terms of Service provide certain rights to users of public repositories, including the ability to view and fork public repositories through GitHub's functionality.

Nothing in this Agreement is intended to override or restrict rights that GitHub grants under its own Terms of Service.

## 5.3 Forks

A GitHub fork created through GitHub's own functionality is governed by the applicable GitHub Terms of Service.

However, creation of a GitHub fork does not grant the forking user any additional license to publish, mirror, redistribute, commercially exploit, or otherwise use the Project outside the rights permitted by GitHub's terms and this Agreement.

Where GitHub's functionality permits a fork, this Agreement does not represent that such platform functionality itself constitutes ownership or a general license to the underlying Project Materials.

## 5.4 Downloading from GitHub

Downloading or accessing files from GitHub does not grant ownership of the files or additional rights beyond those expressly granted by this Agreement, the applicable GitHub Terms of Service, or mandatory applicable law.

