# 11. CONTRIBUTOR OWNERSHIP AND ASSIGNMENT OF RIGHTS

## 11.1 Participation

By submitting or developing a Contribution specifically for the Project, the Contributor agrees to the ownership and rights provisions of this Section to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

## 11.2 Ownership of Contributions

To the extent permitted by applicable law, each Contributor agrees that Contributions specifically created for and submitted to the Project shall become part of the Project and shall be controlled by the Team Leader upon valid assignment or other transfer of the applicable rights.

## 11.3 Assignment of Rights

To the extent that copyright, neighboring rights, database rights, design rights, or other transferable intellectual property rights arise in a Contribution, the Contributor hereby assigns and transfers to the Team Leader, to the fullest extent legally permitted, all transferable rights, title, and interest in that Contribution.

Such rights include, where legally transferable:

a) the right to reproduce;

b) the right to modify and adapt;

c) the right to create derivative works;

d) the right to distribute;

e) the right to publish;

f) the right to display and perform;

g) the right to sublicense;

h) the right to authorize third-party use; and

i) the right to otherwise exploit the Contribution as part of the Project.

## 11.4 Rights That Cannot Be Assigned

Nothing in this Agreement requires a Contributor to transfer or waive any right that cannot legally be assigned or waived under applicable law.

Where such a right cannot be assigned, the Contributor grants the Team Leader, to the fullest extent permitted by law, the broadest applicable license or permission necessary for the Team Leader to develop, modify, distribute, maintain, and otherwise operate the Project.

## 11.5 Contributor's Independent Use

After submission of a Contribution to the Project, the Contributor may not independently extract, publish, license, sell, distribute, or incorporate that Contribution outside the Project where doing so would infringe rights assigned to or controlled by the Team Leader.

This restriction does not apply to:

a) material that the Contributor independently owned before creating the Contribution and did not assign to the Team Leader;

b) Third-Party Content;

c) material released under a separate license that expressly permits such use; or

d) rights that the Contributor is legally unable to assign or restrict.

## 11.6 Pre-Existing Materials

A Contributor remains the owner of materials created before their participation in the Project unless those materials are expressly assigned or licensed to the Team Leader in writing.

If a Contribution contains pre-existing material owned by the Contributor, the Contributor must disclose that fact to the Team Leader before or at the time of submission.

Unless otherwise agreed in writing, submission of such pre-existing material grants the Team Leader a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, transferable, sublicensable license to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, publish, display, perform, and otherwise exploit that material solely as incorporated into the Project and its associated distributions.

## 11.7 Contributor Representations

Each Contributor represents, to the best of their knowledge, that:

a) they have the authority to submit the Contribution;

b) the Contribution does not knowingly infringe another person's rights;

c) any third-party material in the Contribution has been disclosed and is used under appropriate permission or license; and

d) they will not knowingly submit confidential or unauthorized material belonging to another person or organization.

